		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4286&amp;p=32374#p32374"><![CDATA[
The bootloader in the Radioddity GD-77, enumerates as a USB HID device.<br><br>These devices are not easy to see as they are hidden in with the keyboard and mouse devices on a PC<br><br>None of the radios that the OpenGD77 firmware supports, uses a serial / Com port for the firmware update<br><br><br><br>Btw. Did you every run something like Zadig on your PC to swap device drivers, as Zadig can screw up the drivers in the way you described<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Aug 01, 2024 9:50 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
